Unlike in previous versions of Madeline, the program now identifies the
gender and affection status codes used in Linkage files without the user
having to tell it explicitely.  You can prove this to yourself
using the following command:

M>view data sex, _IsFemale, affected, _IsAffected for #true

F0021   K0001A  1       0       0       .
F0021   K0001B  2       1       0       .
F0021   K00158  1       0       1       0
F0021   K00159  1       0       0       .
F0021   K00163  1       0       0       .
F0021   K00164  1       0       1       0
F0021   K00165  1       0       2       1
F0021   K00166  1       0       1       0
F0021   K00169  2       1       0       .
F0021   K00170  1       0       1       0
F0021   K00171  2       1       1       0
F0021   K00172  2       1       1       0
F0021   K00177  1       0       2       1

13 individuals in 1 pedigree matched as follows:

Individuals ..............         13
 + In database ...........         13
 |  + Attached ...........         13
 |  + Childless spouses ..          0
 |  + Unattached .........          0
 + Not in database .......          0
M>

Madeline's correct interpretation of the data is made
possible by the GenderStatus and AffectionStatus arrays:

M>list GenderStatus
GenderStatus has 6 elements:
GenderStatus[1]=0             <-- Linkage-specific
GenderStatus[2]=1             <-- Linkage-specific
GenderStatus["F"]=1
GenderStatus["M"]=0
GenderStatus["♀"]=1
GenderStatus["♂"]=0

M>list AffectionStatus
AffectionStatus has 6 elements:
AffectionStatus[0]=#MISSING
AffectionStatus[1]=0          <-- Linkage-specific
AffectionStatus[2]=1          <-- Linkage-specific
AffectionStatus["A"]=1
AffectionStatus["I"]=#MISSING
AffectionStatus["U"]=0
M>

Please see the full HTML documentation for additional
information.

